# Apply order and USE-flag grouping, mirroring src_prepare() in the overlay's
# single app-editors/zeo ebuild -- resolved, never named. (Until 2026-10-01 the
# series rode app-editors/zed; zed now builds upstream's releases unpatched.) An overlay autoupdate
# bumps that ebuild most days, so a version written here is stale before anyone
# reads it; this header said zed-1.19.0_pre20260826-r1 while the tree packaged
# 1.19.0_pre20260829, three bumps later. `resolve_version` in scripts/lib.sh is
# how the tooling finds it.

# 0018: dropping a folder opens it as its own project, restoring the tabs and
# panel state saved for those paths, instead of adding it to the project already
# open -- which also stops save_workspace's "clear out old workspaces with the
# same paths" DELETE from erasing that saved record on every drag. Behind the
# new drop_folder_behavior setting, defaulting to the behaviour Zed already had,
# so it is UNGROUPED: no USE flag gates it and the ebuild applies it
# unconditionally. Window placement defers to default_open_behavior rather than
# adding a second knob.
0018-drop-folder-opens-project.patch

# 0024: zed://agent?session=<id>[&cwd=<dir>] reopens an existing thread. The
# URL handler accepted only ?prompt=, so a link could start a conversation and
# never return to one. The thread opens the way a sidebar click opens it: the
# agent and folders come off its metadata row, and the window is the one
# holding that project, found across every window -- not the focused one, and
# not AgentPanel::open_thread, which resolves every id to the native agent and
# failed with "no thread found" for the adapter's sessions.
# UNGROUPED like 0018: it needs no adapter and changes no default, so no USE
# flag gates it. Numbered 0024 because 0019-0023 are the zeo rebrand patches,
# which share this directory and this number space.
0024-agent-deep-link-session.patch

# 0019-0023, 0025, 0032: the rebrand -- what makes this package Zeo rather than Zed.
# UNGROUPED: without them this ebuild would build Zed under another name. They
# apply BEFORE every USE group, so their diff never depends on which flags are
# set; the feature patches below are regenerated on top of them.
0019-paths-use-Zeo-state-directories.patch
0020-zed-name-the-application-binary-zeo.patch
0021-release_channel-add-the-Zeo-channel.patch
0022-zed-register-zeo-and-keep-accepting-zed.patch
0023-cli-point-the-launcher-at-the-Zeo-application-binary.patch
0025-zed-say-Zeo-in-the-strings-a-user-actually-reads.patch
# 0032: the Flatpak escape (the CLI re-executing itself on the host through
# flatpak-spawn) was keyed on Zed's app id and binary names, so it never fired
# for dev.zeo.Zeo. Rebrand, so ungrouped; inert outside a Flatpak.
0032-cli-let-the-Flatpak-escape-recognise-Zeo-s-app-id-an.patch

# 0033: Claude Agent (Plus) and Claude Agent TUI ship as default agents -- npx
# entries added to the ACP registry list and enabled in default.json, always
# @latest from npm, installed by Zeo's own Node runtime on first use. A Zeo
# feature with no adapter dependency at build time, so UNGROUPED.
0033-agent-ship-Claude-Agent-Plus-and-Claude-Agent-TUI-as-default.patch

# @feature: claude-agent-acp-plus
0001-force-enable-claude-agent-acp-plus.patch
# 0003/0004 (per-option _meta description + preview) retired: upstream 950ec79
# surfaces option descriptions natively via the ACP EnumOption.description
# field, superseding the _claude/askUserQuestionOption _meta machinery (and
# renamed MultiSelectItems::Untitled -> String). The numbers stay retired so
# the remaining filenames keep matching the ebuild's PATCHES+=() lines.
0005-elicitation-multiline-fields.patch
0006-elicitation-option-previews.patch
0007-manual-mode-badge.patch
0008-clickable-attachments.patch
# 0009 (adopt the agent's config-option response when applying per-agent
# defaults) retired: upstream 78a0da201 (#65233) routes the defaults path through
# ConfigOptions::set_config_option, which installs the agent's returned option
# list and wakes the config-options watch -- the same fix, with upstream tests
# for options that appear after a dependent default.
# 0010: a thread menu choice (permission mode, model, thinking effort, an ACP
# agent's config options) applies to that thread only; Shift also makes it the
# default for new threads. It applies to the packaged source on its own, so it
# rides this flag by choice rather than by dependency -- it also covers the
# native agent's own menus, which this flag otherwise has nothing to do with.
0010-shift-to-set-as-default.patch
# 0011: an "Account" section in the context tooltip, showing the account quota
# windows (5-hour, weekly, per-model) the adapter already forwards under
# _meta["_claude/rateLimit"] and Zed previously discarded. It rides this flag by
# dependency, not by choice: no other agent sends that key, so without the
# adapter the section never renders.
0011-account-usage-panel.patch
# 0012: a "Worktrees" entry in the agent panel's menu, dispatching the existing
# zero-argument zed_actions::git::Worktree so the picker decides between creating
# a worktree and switching to one. Zed already ships the capability end to end and
# the panel already reaches it -- but only under request.use_new_worktree, which is
# an input of the create_thread AGENT TOOL, so the model could open a worktree and
# the person looking at the same panel could not. It applies to the packaged source
# on its own, so like 0010 it rides this flag by choice rather than by dependency:
# nothing about a worktree needs the adapter.
0012-agent-panel-worktree-entry.patch
# 0013: the model-scoped quota window. The adapter forwards every
# rate_limits.model_scoped[] entry under the single wire kind "model_scoped",
# and from_wire had no arm for it, so the per-model row 0011's Account section
# was built to show never arrived. Adds a dynamic variant carrying the
# server-supplied display name -- it adds a name, it does not open the enum:
# an unrecognised kind is still dropped. Rides this flag BY DEPENDENCY, like
# 0011: no other agent sends that key.
0013-model-scoped-quota-window.patch
# 0014: a copy button on the user's own message, returning the string the edit
# path already serialises (ContentBlock::to_markdown, what the LostFocus handler
# compares against) rather than a second serialisation. The button sits on the
# shared container before the editable/non-editable branch, so subagent messages
# -- always non-editable -- get it too. Pure Zed affordance, so it rides this
# flag BY CHOICE, the way 0010 and 0012 do.
0014-copy-the-user-s-own-message.patch
# 0015: the thread archive scoped to its project. Three reads were global, not
# one: the list, the ArchivedOnly fall-back guard, and the archived-only
# toggle's own disabled state. Deliberately NOT via the store's entries_for_path
# -- that reader drops archived threads, which is correct for the sidebar and
# fatal for an archive view. Pure Zed, BY CHOICE.
0015-scoped-thread-history.patch
# 0016: a rendered-markdown preview of the composer's draft, through the same
# MarkdownElement that draws every agent response. Reached by the
# ToggleMessagePreview action (command palette; bindable). The source is
# re-derived on each toggle and refreshed on edit -- an Entity<Markdown> built
# once renders the first draft forever while passing every two-step test. Pure
# Zed, BY CHOICE, and the only one of the five that is new UI rather than an
# affordance over existing machinery.
0016-composer-markdown-preview.patch
# 0017: native rendering for a compaction the adapter reports. NOT because the
# ACP notification is unreachable -- that was this comment's claim until
# 2026-09-22 and it was false; acp_thread.rs matches
# acp::SessionUpdate::CompactionUpdate and the linked crate is 2.2.0 / schema
# 1.9.1. It is because _meta.contextCompaction is the channel the adapter
# actually sends, so this reads that versioned key and dispatches into the
# EXISTING push_context_compaction. An unknown version falls through to the
# generic tool row untouched. Both the opening and terminal frames are consumed
# at the same seam, or update_tool_call fabricates a "Tool call not found"
# failure row beside the entry. Rides this flag BY DEPENDENCY: only this adapter
# emits that key.
0017-native-compaction-entry.patch
# 0026: the thread's controls -- copy, previous user message, top, bottom --
# float over the conversation instead of riding inside the last list item,
# where they scrolled out of view together with the turn that owned them. Copy
# and "previous user message" are read off the scroll position: copy takes the
# turn under the overlay (disabled while that turn is still in progress), and
# each click on the other lands one user message earlier. Pure Zed, BY CHOICE,
# the way 0010, 0012 and 0014 are.
0026-float-thread-navigation-controls.patch
# 0027: a question the agent asks is pinned above the composer instead of
# scrolling away with the conversation, and a multi-question one is stepped
# through a page at a time. Both halves reuse what is already here: Zed
# already renders the CONNECTION-scoped elicitations in that exact slot, with
# this exact card, and only the SESSION-scoped half -- which is how
# AskUserQuestion arrives -- never reached it. Behind the new
# agent.elicitation_placement setting, offered as two entries in the panel's
# options menu; unlike 0018 it defaults to the NEW behaviour, with upstream's
# inline rendering one click away. Pagination is gated on the adapter's
# un-namespaced _askUserQuestionCustomAnswer marker, so an MCP server's
# ordinary form is never split. Several question sets asked in one turn are
# queued in that one card -- "Set 1 of 3", the next taking the card as each is
# answered -- rather than stacked; permissions stay stacked. Rides this flag
# BY CHOICE, like 0010, 0012,
# 0014 and 0026: the elicitation path is generic ACP and nothing here needs
# the adapter -- but nothing else in practice sends a question-shaped form.
0027-pinned-elicitation-card.patch
# 0028: a folder dropped on the threads sidebar opens as a project of its own,
# through the same MultiWorkspace::open_project the sidebar's "Add Project"
# popover uses -- one project per folder, files ignored, and a folder that is
# already a project in any window skipped rather than re-activated. The sidebar
# accepted no drop before, so there is no old behaviour to keep behind a
# setting. Pure Zed, BY CHOICE, the way 0014 and 0026 are: the threads sidebar
# is agent UI, and nothing here needs the adapter.
0028-sidebar-drop-folder-adds-project.patch
# 0029: a thread whose turn has ended while a background shell or async
# subagent keeps running gets its own sidebar status -- the running-turn
# spinner, tinted and slower -- instead of falling back to the agent's plain
# icon. The count arrives as _meta["_claude/backgroundTasks"] on a
# session_info_update, the SDK's background_tasks_changed level minus its
# ambient tasks, and it arrives between turns, which is the whole point. Rides
# this flag BY DEPENDENCY, like 0011 and 0013: no other agent sends that key.
0029-background-task-status.patch
# 0030: a thread whose agent asked a question and is waiting for the answer
# gets its own sidebar status -- a Chat icon and "Waiting for Your Answer" --
# instead of the running spinner the still-open turn produced. Reads the
# Conversation's elicitation_requests map, which was kept up to date and read
# by nothing; permissions keep their warning triangle and outrank it. Pure
# Zed and generic ACP, so it rides this flag BY CHOICE, like 0027.
0030-question-status.patch
# 0031: the turn stats gain the session's side -- the turn's duration always
# shown, a running total of agent time since the thread was opened in this
# window, and a tool-call count whose tooltip breaks it down by tool, by MCP
# server and by the programs the terminal calls ran. Same row, same
# show_turn_stats setting; the total lives on the view and restarts when the
# thread is reopened. Pure Zed and generic ACP, BY CHOICE, like 0026.
0031-session-stats.patch
# 0036: a reopened ACP thread comes back in the config it was left in --
# mode, model, effort and every other option -- instead of being reset to the
# entry's default_config_options on session/load or session/resume. The last
# state the client saw is recorded per (agent, session) in the key-value store
# upstream ships, namespace acp_thread_config, with no migration; a value the
# agent no longer offers falls back to the default with a log line, and a new
# or forked thread still starts from the defaults. Generic ACP, so it rides
# this flag BY CHOICE, like 0010.
0036-thread-config-survives-reopen.patch
# 0034: the agent's task feed -- AcpThread holds the adapter's
# _meta["_claude/tasks"] snapshot (every live task, replaced, never merged),
# announces each ending once, keeps a thread with running tasks out of idle
# eviction, and carries _claude/tasks/stop and /background over the
# connection, gated on the agent advertising the capability. 0029's count
# keeps its own key. Model only; the card and the panel come later. Rides
# this flag BY DEPENDENCY, like 0011, 0013 and 0029: no other agent sends it.
0034-agent-task-feed.patch
# 0037: the tasks card -- a floating card over the agent panel listing the
# live tasks of every conversation the panel holds, grouped by thread, with
# Stop (confirmed), Send to Background, Open at the tool call that started it,
# and Watch. Behind agent.tasks_card.{enabled, position}, defaulting to on and
# top_right; with no task it draws nothing. Also touches upstream's NewEntry
# catch-up in conversation_view.rs and makes open_thread_by_session reactivate
# a conversation the panel already holds. Rides this flag BY DEPENDENCY, like
# 0034 under it: only this adapter sends _claude/tasks, and only from 0.24.0 --
# against the released 0.23.6 the card stays empty.
0037-tasks-card.patch
# 0038: a watched or failed task that ends out of view is sent to zeo-systray
# as one non-blocking datagram on $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/zeo-systray.sock (never
# /tmp), eight fields, no model-written text. The daemon is optional at
# runtime (>= 0.3.0 parses it); without it the send is a silent no-op. Rides
# this flag BY DEPENDENCY, with 0037.
0038-tasks-card-tray.patch
# 0035: the Agent Tasks panel -- a dock panel (left, 320 px) listing every
# task the agent ran, grouped by thread, with Active/Finished/Failed/Archived
# filters, Stop through the card's confirmation, and archive. The history
# lives in its own sqlez domain, AgentTaskHistoryDb, with an append-only
# migration list; running rows are swept to interrupted at startup, and a
# database that fails to open leaves the panel saying the history is
# unavailable. agent_tasks_panel::ToggleFocus on ctrl-alt-shift-a /
# cmd-alt-shift-a; no settings of its own. Rides this flag BY DEPENDENCY,
# after 0038: fed only by 0037's card, so by claude-agent-acp-plus >= 0.24.0.
0035-agent-tasks-panel.patch
# after 0035: one-line labels in 0037's card and 0035's panel, and the panel's Rename (story 022).
0039-agent-task-labels.patch
# 0040: one router, agent_ui::open_agent_session, opens a session in the
# window that holds its project's folders (exact set, else a new window),
# raising it; the tray link (0024) and the Agent Tasks panel (0035) both call
# it, and the panel no longer re-enters itself from its click listener
# (story 024). After 0035 and 0039, whose open_task and rows it changes, so
# it rides this flag BY DEPENDENCY.
0040-agent-route-sessions-to-their-project-window.patch
# 0041: every running row of 0037's card shows its last tool and tool count;
# 0035's history keeps the tool call that started each task (a migration step
# appended after 0039's) and "Open at Task" opens the thread through 0040's
# router scrolled to it (story 023). After 0040, whose reserved tool_call_id it
# honours, so it rides this flag BY DEPENDENCY.
0041-agent-tasks-progress-and-open-at-task.patch
# 0042: an archived record of 0035's Agent Tasks panel can be deleted -- one
# row's Delete, or Delete All Archived under the Archived filter -- after a
# confirmation; only the history row goes, the thread is never touched. No
# migration. After 0041, whose panel and history it changes, so it rides this
# flag BY DEPENDENCY (story 025).
0042-agent-tasks-panel-delete-archived.patch

